	(text "The floppy interface, as rev B. Inputs: a 10k pull-up to 3.3 V always, and a 1k to PC_TERM, which J7's\njumper joins to 3.3 V for a real PC (909 R); then 1k in series to the GPIO (R47-R56), which limits the\ncurrent a host driving a line high can push into the RP2350 while it's unpowered (under 5 mA).\nOutputs: through the SN7407 (open collector); GPIO low asserts.\nGate 6 drives pin 2 (/CHNG for Shugart and Amiga hosts, pin02=chg): the rework rev B needed.\nPins 4 and 6 are read only (GPIO 36, 42), for hosts that use them: 10k pull-up, 1k series."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 20 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3e09e98f-4ad9-5037-9c05-3996a6ed27f8")
	)
